493 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 193 0 R
/E (Mr. Davis begins his fifth-grade math lesson on calculating the area of a triangle by showing a picture of the Great Pyramid of Giza and asking his students how much stone it took to cover the sides, successfully gaining their attention. He then informs them of the lesson objectives for by writing on the board that they will learn how to find the area of any triangle using a formula. To stimulate recall, he quickly reminds the class that they learned how to find the area of a rectangle using length times width the previous week. Next, he presents the new material for by introducing the triangle area formula and writing out two step-by-step examples on the whiteboard. He hands out a worksheet with ten triangles and instructs the students to spend fifteen minutes solving them on their own. As they work, he provides formative feedback for by walking around the room to offer immediate corrections and praise. Finally, to assess performance, he has the students independently complete a two-question Exit Ticket at the end of class.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
